{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:d974c1697e8f9caef19885bdf7019664a20ae5286f35f90df703b1e63947fb82","title":"The proposed extension seeks Higgs-mass stabilization by adding higher derivative kinetic operators throughout the Standard Model. Each operator introduces a massive resonance rather than a new stable asymptotic particle, with its mass initially independent of the masses in other representations.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d91d87eadfcb5f722d7093947d0839dc8b5f27f988cd49fed068a303a3ec4838","title":"Do nongeometric fluxes possess source solitons analogous to NS5 and KK5 objects, and can their contributions relax the corresponding flux constraints? The paper poses this as an unresolved extension.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d9136329992bf801a7cf8481b6eddbfc3204a68002927071cea7392f23738902","title":"Can an earlier accelerating epoch dynamically prepare the spatial flatness and causal correlations required by the later hot Big Bang?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0003"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d9490acc22f0a18b52d9d4089cf1a9ec07fde2ac200cb93ef899a942488ff9ba","title":"Review how anisotropic spatial derivatives motivate Hořava–Lifshitz gravity and assess the viability of its projectable version, particularly its additional scalar degree of freedom.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:d9557666a7c251a9d727b63ea3886723b0573c011a3f1760631b44620afbda81","title":"How should classical and quantum vacuum contributions to the cosmological constant be defined and renormalized, and why does a discrepancy with gravitational observations remain afte